#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167137 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166885 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4e5deee-e910-5bb1-9d9a-0b24886ab6c1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Polar Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c1ea06c-900b-518b-90c1-188a82af18c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163902} {:answer/id #uuid "4486d7e0-2a87-59a4-9e31-7eb1fae5055e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163904} {:answer/id #uuid "3243821a-d8ad-5dd7-aced-e15740550519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480836} {:answer/id #uuid "932abe94-bffd-5dad-a100-ed7dd0878970" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481015} {:answer/id #uuid "a461f542-25f5-59e6-a3ba-329bd57b7ee7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "932abe94-bffd-5dad-a100-ed7dd0878970" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481015} :answer-field/id #uuid "a885e1f2-0379-5509-836d-b0ab6acba537" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163900}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e7ccaa25-bf49-56f7-93ee-b9d797d03126" :question/math-academy-id "q-163068" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x,y)=2x+y$ on the portion of the disk of radius $2$ centered at the origin, where $y\\ge 0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region $D:$ \n\n![](images/b5/b5ba69ab02aa13e201b7b9113f6a36e705ad19e6412499504afc4f239459a8f3.png)\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}=2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe average value of the function over a region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi \\}.\n$$\n\nUsing the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(2x+y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}(2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{2}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ){\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,{[\\frac{{r}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )(\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3}-0)\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ]_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}((2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ))-(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}(1+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{16}{3}=\\frac{8}{3\\pi }.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481411 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166884 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b43eea5b-9da3-5fe0-a28c-cc01aed3627a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b7b96a3-3ee8-51d8-bf7e-f10bc137dc77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480796} {:answer/id #uuid "5ea1906a-4d23-5e92-aa42-2516002c4c66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480915} {:answer/id #uuid "654022a5-61f4-581f-8b07-c11340a40a55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480925} {:answer/id #uuid "e98d6b52-9796-58a4-ba09-031961cb2020" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481186} {:answer/id #uuid "fc2a60a5-710d-5d16-938e-a0bd54aeac9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "654022a5-61f4-581f-8b07-c11340a40a55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480925} :answer-field/id #uuid "da8ec83a-e269-5c73-bf54-b07a27aefc49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bbfd9077-09aa-55c5-a7ec-ce238f7922af" :question/math-academy-id "q-163240" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x,y)=y+{x}^{2}$ on the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,x\\le y\\le 2x\\}$ given that the area of the region is $2.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{∬}_{D}y+{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x}^{2x}y+{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+{x}^{2}y]_{y=x}^{y=2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{x}^{3}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}]_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(8-0) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281649 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166884 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b43eea5b-9da3-5fe0-a28c-cc01aed3627a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c9c1a55-bba0-56ad-b34a-3f8e8d7f257c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278854} {:answer/id #uuid "626dc16f-8c1c-5295-aa50-90b66258e711" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279486} {:answer/id #uuid "67ad624f-1636-5880-94a3-08d7d29a2390" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279534} {:answer/id #uuid "d1e6422b-62b6-59e0-932d-a0c2aeb5b3e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280446} {:answer/id #uuid "d4cb2768-4bcd-5b37-aeef-50e75f09d3ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280468}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "626dc16f-8c1c-5295-aa50-90b66258e711" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279486} :answer-field/id #uuid "08429d71-a216-5cf2-b30e-790877dfd6fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280845}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "94920c42-c29f-5248-bff0-1bbc9f005b27" :question/math-academy-id "q-163246" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x,y)=2x+3{y}^{2}$ on the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that \n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=1\\cdot 2=2.\n$$\n\nApplying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{∬}_{D}(2x+3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(2x+3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[2xy+{y}^{3}]_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4x+8)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[2{x}^{2}+8x]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\cdot {1}^{2}+8\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{2} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481357 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166885 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4e5deee-e910-5bb1-9d9a-0b24886ab6c1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Polar Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e360105-eb66-5367-814d-689677702f6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480975} {:answer/id #uuid "9e9f7126-1aec-56cb-a084-4f34d28dafc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481043} {:answer/id #uuid "a79440e4-ebcc-5811-a667-c1e64c7db96b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481055} {:answer/id #uuid "c27b400b-e962-57cc-9be7-11f6f93220fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481111} {:answer/id #uuid "d99527b4-de43-5d96-9eda-144ff935847e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e360105-eb66-5367-814d-689677702f6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480975} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a10b6cc-8155-5c1e-bf70-aecfcd94d2ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481254}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3b9226c2-67e0-5858-9c64-ae46c4147a95" :question/math-academy-id "q-163257" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x,y)={y}^{2}$ on the disk of radius $2$ centered at the origin." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that \n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}=4\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe average value of the function over a region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi \\}.\n$$\n\nUsing the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,{[\\frac{{r}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta (4-0)\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{[\\theta -\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =2[(2\\pi -0)-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0)] \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =4\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{1}{4\\pi }\\cdot 4\\pi =1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281662 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166885 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4e5deee-e910-5bb1-9d9a-0b24886ab6c1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Polar Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27060319-319a-5c93-87a4-021b464e69b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278938} {:answer/id #uuid "96cddbff-aa96-5c15-b451-85bc3b5899ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279926} {:answer/id #uuid "d6297845-0a0a-51e3-9056-3d94de569441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280482} {:answer/id #uuid "d932caf8-3377-5328-b82d-2c72ffe1d077" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280511} {:answer/id #uuid "fb6871d0-cf0d-5786-9a5c-fd24e0463ae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb6871d0-cf0d-5786-9a5c-fd24e0463ae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280794} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4bf3c23-4651-531a-8ea1-05778a87081e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4da84d34-65b6-5264-9689-a8f568b0485b" :question/math-academy-id "q-163278" :question/problem "![](images/f8/f84a8fcd4ed668a6b94d5b084ade49dc8fc027feff4baea862e2feaf68221534.png)\n\nFind the average value of the function $f(x,y)=y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ on the semicircle shown above." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that \n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot {1}^{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nThe average value of the function over a region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nNotice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $1$ centered at \n$(-1,0).$\n\nCartesian and polar coordinates are connected by the following equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\\\ y &=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the $y=\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-2x}$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}-2x} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-{x}^{2}-2x \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =-2x \\\\ (r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2} & =-2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) & =-2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {r}^{2} & =-2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {r}^{2}+2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ r(r+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire semicircle, we must have $r=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .$\n\nTherefore, in polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\sqrt{(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta [\\frac{{r}^{4}}{4}]_{0}^{-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ((-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{4}-{0}^{4})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{4}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =4{[-\\frac{{cos}^{5}⁡\\theta }{5}]}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}({cos}^{5}⁡\\pi -{cos}^{5}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{ave}}=\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}\\cdot \\frac{4}{5}=\\frac{8}{5\\pi }.\n$$"}]}
